Output of bentoolkit's `bentoo notice new` renderer (internal/notice
RenderSiteYAML, bentoolkit commit c204a7f), read by
tests/unit/consumer-contract-extra.test.ts through the site's notices loader.

- 2026-10-02-foo-cve.yaml: a byte-for-byte copy of bentoolkit's
  internal/notice/testdata/site.golden.yaml (the renderer's own golden).
  Re-copy it when that file changes; `cmp` shows drift.
- The other three files were rendered on 2026-09-29 by that commit's
  render_site.go, unchanged, from the Notice values listed in the test
  (WRITTEN). They pin the shapes the golden does not reach: the
  double-quoted body with \L/\P escapes and with a leading line feed,
  a tab-led literal body line, quoted free text that a plain scalar would
  retype, a range-less entry and an `updated` off midnight (a revision).

These are not site notices: the site never builds from this directory.
